Vendored Android runtime sources from:
https://github.com/mcginty/blew/tree/blew-v0.5.1-beta.8 (crates/blew/android)
First vendored at blew-v0.3.0 in July 2026; rebased onto blew-v0.5.1-beta.8 on 2026-11-02.

Files (modules/iroh-location/android/src/main/java/org/jakebot/blew/):
- AdapterRename.kt
- BleCentralManager.kt
- BlePeripheralManager.kt
- GattConnections.kt
- GattOperationQueue.kt
- GattServerHost.kt
- L2capSocketManager.kt
- Subscription.kt

Upstream's BlewPlugin.kt (the Tauri plugin entry point) and its Kotlin unit tests are
not vendored.

License: AGPL-3.0-or-later (see LICENSE in this directory).

The files are copied into the IrohLocation Expo module because the Rust `blew`
backend requires Android Kotlin managers and JNI callbacks in the application
classloader.

Modifications by the streetCryptid project
------------------------------------------

2026-10-31 (on 0.3.0): BlePeripheralManager.startAdvertising no longer renamed the
Bluetooth adapter to the advertised local name. Upstream 0.4 made the name optional
(`LocalName::None` is the default and what this app uses), so on 0.5.1-beta.8 this file
is upstream's own.

2026-10-31: request CONNECTION_PRIORITY_HIGH on every central connection, after the
MTU exchange. On 0.5.1-beta.8 this lives in GattConnections.kt, where the connection
attempt now completes.

The Rust half of blew is vendored too, since 2026-10-31, at
modules/iroh-location/rust/third_party/blew/ (with its own NOTICE).
